    {
      "text": "(higher is better). Bottom row plots show cost (lower is better). RESPO (red curve) achieves best balance of",
      "bbox": [
        107.70397186279297,
        227.40478515625,
        503.9976806640625,
        235.42074584960938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "maximizing reward and minimizing cost. RCRL framework implemented with our REF without V π",
      "bbox": [
        107.99996948242188,
        235.48851013183594,
        461.9546813964844,
        245.38272094726562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "c incurs very",
      "bbox": [
        455.56097412109375,
        237.36676025390625,
        504.3160400390625,
        246.96072387695312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "high costs. PPOLag in CMDP framework with χ = 0 has very low reward performance. So, learning REF and",
      "bbox": [
        107.99996948242188,
        247.18630981445312,
        504.0044250488281,
        255.34573364257812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
