      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Discussion and Conclusion",
      "bbox": [
        125.93276977539062,
        322.3209228515625,
        262.1264343261719,
        333.0686340332031
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In summary, we proposed a new optimization formulation and a class of algorithms for safety-",
      "bbox": [
        107.99996948242188,
        346.9283752441406,
        505.6536560058594,
        355.8349304199219
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "constrained reinforcement learning. Our framework optimizes reward performance for states in",
      "bbox": [
        107.99996948242188,
        357.8373718261719,
        503.9974670410156,
        366.7439270019531
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "least-violation policy’s feasible state space while maintaining persistent safety as well as providing",
      "bbox": [
        107.99996948242188,
        368.7463684082031,
        504.0042724609375,
        377.6529235839844
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the safest behavior in other states by ensuring entrance into the feasible set with minimal cumulative",
      "bbox": [
        107.99996948242188,
        379.6553649902344,
        503.99847412109375,
        388.5619201660156
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "discounted costs. Using our proposed reachability estimation function, we prove our algorithm’s class",
      "bbox": [
        107.99996948242188,
        390.5643615722656,
        504.00140380859375,
        399.4709167480469
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "of actor-critic methods converge a locally optimal policy for our proposed optimization. We provide",
      "bbox": [
        107.99996948242188,
        401.4733581542969,
        504.0012512207031,
        410.3799133300781
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "extensive experimental results on a diverse suite of environments in Safety Gym, PyBullet, and",
      "bbox": [
        107.99996948242188,
        412.3823547363281,
        503.997314453125,
        421.2889099121094
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "MuJoCo, and an environment with multiple hard and soft constraints, to demonstrate the effectiveness",
      "bbox": [
        107.99996948242188,
        423.2923583984375,
        504.00146484375,
        432.19891357421875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "of our algorithm when compared with several SOTA baselines. We leave open various extensions to",
      "bbox": [
        107.99996948242188,
        434.20135498046875,
        503.9959716796875,
        443.10791015625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "our work to enable real-world deployment of our algorithm. These include constraining violations",
      "bbox": [
        107.99996948242188,
        445.1103515625,
        503.9978332519531,
        454.01690673828125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "during training, guaranteeing safety in single-lifetime reinforcement learning, and ensuring policies",
      "bbox": [
        107.99996948242188,
        456.01934814453125,
        503.995849609375,
        464.9259033203125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "don’t forget feasible sets as environment tasks change. Our approach of learning the optimal REF",
      "bbox": [
        107.99996948242188,
        466.9283752441406,
        504.2819519042969,
        475.8349304199219
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "to reduce the state space into a low-dimensional likelihood representation to guide training for",
      "bbox": [
        107.99996948242188,
        477.8373718261719,
        504.16998291015625,
        486.7439270019531
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "high-dimensional policies can have applications in other learning problems in answering binary",
      "bbox": [
        107.99996948242188,
        488.7463684082031,
        504.3428955078125,
        497.6529235839844
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "classification or likelihood-based questions about dynamics in high-dimension feature spaces.",
      "bbox": [
        107.99996948242188,
        499.6553649902344,
        481.4579162597656,
        508.5619201660156
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
